    "q-106963": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106963",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}.\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of ${u}_{33}$ in the matrix $U?$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 18 & -19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 18 & -26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${u}_{33}=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
