      "knowledge_point": "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization",
      "kp_id": "e-4772"
    },
    "q-106968": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106968",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 36 & -32 & 46\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $-4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -32 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(-4)=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
