      "problem": "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ \\,\\,4\\,\\, & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-4$ and ${u}_{22}=-4,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
