    "q-106972": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106972",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & \\,2\\, & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=2$ and ${u}_{23}=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{23}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
