    "q-32742": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32742",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $C=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $C$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -6 & -7 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & -\\frac{1}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${u}_{22}=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (-6)=3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
