    "q-32748": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32748",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -16 & 16 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 & 17\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $B=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $B$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{42}\\cdot {u}_{34}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $B$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -9 & -16 & 16 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,4\\,\\, & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{42}=-5$ and ${u}_{34}=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{42}\\cdot {u}_{33}=(-5)\\cdot 1=-5.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
