    "q-107065": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107065",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -8 & 11 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $C=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $C$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{41}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -8 & 11 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -32 & 51 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -32 & 51 & 11 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -8 & -4 & 11 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -8 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{41}=-2$ and ${u}_{33}=11,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{41}\\cdot {u}_{33}=(-2)\\cdot 11=-22.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
